From: SF2000 Linux <sf2000@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qpsx: complete out-of-band libretro state loads

rcntFreezeLoaded exists to stop psxRcntUpdate when the SDL frontend loads a
state recursively from EmuUpdate.  A libretro unserialize call happens while
CPU execution is already paused.  Leaving the recursive-load guard armed in
that case makes the first resumed VBlank return before it advances and
reschedules the root counter; the following Execute call then stalls.

Expose a narrowly named completion hook and call it only after a successful
memory-backed libretro load.  Native in-VBlank loads keep their existing
guard semantics.

--- a/src/psxcounters.h
+++ b/src/psxcounters.h
@@ -52,5 +52,6 @@ u32 psxRcntRtarget(u32 index);
 
 int psxRcntFreeze(void* f, FreezeMode mode);
 void psxRcntInitFromFreeze(void);
+void psxRcntCompleteExternalFreeze(void);
 
 void psxRcntAdjustTimestamps(const uint32_t prev_cycle_val);
--- a/src/psxcounters.cpp
+++ b/src/psxcounters.cpp
@@ -618,6 +618,11 @@ void psxRcntInitFromFreeze(void)
 	rcntFreezeLoaded = true;
 }
 
+void psxRcntCompleteExternalFreeze(void)
+{
+	rcntFreezeLoaded = false;
+}
+
 /******************************************************************************/
 // Called before psxRegs.cycle is adjusted back to zero
 //  by PSXINT_RESET_CYCLE_VAL event in psxevents.cpp
--- a/libretro/core/libretro-core.cpp
+++ b/libretro/core/libretro-core.cpp
@@ -4057,6 +4057,8 @@ static int mem_state_run_load(const unsigned char *data, unsigned long capacity)
   SaveFuncs = mem_state_funcs();
   result = LoadState("");
   SaveFuncs = saved;
+  if (result == 0)
+    psxRcntCompleteExternalFreeze();
   return result;
 }
